CorvCAD patch series for KiCad 10.0.6 (caf7377), on top of 0010: let KiCad's NGSPICE wrapper use
a statically linked ngspice.

Applied by integrations/kicad_core/fetch.py. Nothing changes in KiCad's own builds: the new code
is compiled only with CORVCAD_NGSPICE_STATIC defined.

NGSPICE::init_dll loads libngspice at run time with wxDynamicLibrary, looks its functions up by
name, then sources a spinit script that loads the XSPICE code models (.cm plug-ins). An iPadOS
app can't load a library at run time. With CORVCAD_NGSPICE_STATIC, init_dll takes the same
functions from the linked library (integrations/kicad_core/ngspice_ios.sh) and calls
corvcad_ngspice_codemodels(), which registers the code models linked into it, in place of the
spinit search. The rest of init_dll (noaskquit, nomoremode, the empty first circuit) and every
other NGSPICE member are unchanged.
diff --git a/eeschema/sim/ngspice.cpp b/eeschema/sim/ngspice.cpp
index 4ae94f1..41aa8be 100644
--- a/eeschema/sim/ngspice.cpp
+++ b/eeschema/sim/ngspice.cpp
@@ -54,6 +54,14 @@
 #include <pthread.h>
 #endif
 
+#ifdef CORVCAD_NGSPICE_STATIC
+// CorvCAD: registers the XSPICE code models linked into the static ngspice library
+// (integrations/kicad_core/ngspice/static_codemodels.c). That library is built with XSPICE, so
+// it has ngCM_Input_Path, which sharedspice.h declares only when XSPICE is defined.
+extern "C" int corvcad_ngspice_codemodels( void );
+extern "C" char* ngCM_Input_Path( const char* path );
+#endif
+
 
 /**
  * Flag to enable debug output of Ngspice simulator.
